Jqw","review_id":"wwMusQQ19fAYelKul3TFaQ","date":"2010-12-01T04:26:58","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9151403903961182,"text_excerpt":"My fave po-boy joint. Love the roast beef po-boy. I've been getting it for years. Also d'lish... dinner & lunch plates which are super cheap. The seafood po-boys are yummy too. Gotta love the Barq's"},{"business_id":"xU4K9Omt5ydLIaUPFQbJqw","review_id":"Z0LqNHUg32om_b5xIkvsEA","date":"2011-07-25T00:01:10","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9018722176551819,"text_excerpt":"i love this mom and pop po-boy shop one of the best roast beef po-boy ever.the staff is very nice.i took my kids with me for lunch.well my daughter is very picky and she didn't want to there.so they gave her pie to eat a piece of cake.just to make her happy i thought that was very nice"},{"business_id":"xU4K9Omt5ydLIaUPFQbJqw","review_id":"dyRUKwm7LBLbN2puQ2e7cA","date":"2013-04-17T20:39:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8923106789588928,"text_excerpt":"I've been twice and both times for plate lunches, one a really big plate of white beans with a large pork chop and the other a salisbury-steak kind of dish with macaroni and cheese. If you are entertaining your cardiologist or a Top Chef producer for dinner, go elsewhere; there's plenty of calories in them there piles of food and the decor is well-worn by time. But as others here have noted, it seems clean enough even if the paint is bit yellowed and the staff is very friendly."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"xU4K9Omt5ydLIaUPFQbJqw","photo_id":"g-ay9K4ZYDds_d1tFezRLQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/g-ay9K4ZYDds_d1tFezRLQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
